/// What a row in `users` is allowed to be.
///
/// There is deliberately no CUSTOMER here. `users` is the STAFF table: every
/// row in it is somebody who works on the business. Shoppers live in their own
/// table with their own lifecycle, their own credentials and their own
/// sessions — see docs/decisions.md §2 for why the two cannot be one table.
///
/// The shape of this enum is therefore load-bearing, not cosmetic. Adding a
/// CUSTOMER value back would silently re-create the single-account model the
/// split exists to avoid, and would do it without a schema review, because
/// every `Record<Role, …>` in src/ would still compile.
enum Role {
  STAFF
  ADMIN
}
